gafR(){return"This star is misplaced: it isn't part of the solution. Remove it."},
gafJ(){return"This cell was wrongly marked as not-a-star: it should hold a star."},
gafB(){return"Mark this cell as not a star: it touches a star that's already placed."},
afG(a){return"Mark this cell as not a star: this "+a+" already has all its stars."},
afI(a){return"Place a star here: it's the only cell left in this "+a+" for its remaining star."},
gafK(){return"Place a star here: it's the next star of the solution."},
afL(a){return"Mark this cell as not a star: the highlighted cells belong to a region with nowhere left to go, so it will take every star this "+a+" has room for."},
afH(a){return"Mark this cell as not a star: the highlighted "+a+" can only take its stars from this region, using up every one it has left."},
gafF(){return"Mark this cell as not a star: whichever way the grid is finished, no solution ever puts a star here. No simple rule shows it \u2014 this one takes several steps of reasoning."},
afE(a){return"Mark this cell as not a star: try a star here and keep applying the basic rules \u2014 it cascades into a dead end where the highlighted "+a+" has nowhere left to put its stars."},
afQ(a){return"Mark this cell as not a star: a star here would block so many cells that the highlighted "+a+" would no longer have room for the stars it still needs."},
afM(a){return"Mark this cell as not a star: it touches every cell where this "+a+" can still place a star, so it would end up next to whichever one gets it."},
